WEBVTT

00:04:29.833 --> 00:04:31.851
is seemingly simple.

00:04:31.875 --> 00:04:33.643
We start with a solution

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:37.059
of positively charged copper spheres.

00:04:37.083 --> 00:04:41.518
We then add to it an insulating
printed circuit board.

00:04:41.542 --> 00:04:44.934
And we feed those
positively charged spheres

00:04:44.958 --> 00:04:46.726
negatively charged electrons

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:49.143
by adding formaldehyde to the mix.

00:04:49.167 --> 00:04:50.934
So you might remember formaldehyde.

00:04:50.958 --> 00:04:52.726
Really distinct odor,

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:56.059
used to preserve frogs in biology class.

00:04:56.083 --> 00:04:58.851
Well it turns out it can do
a lot more than just that.

00:04:58.875 --> 00:05:00.934
And it's a really key component